        <description>
            Stereo CAmeras for Lunar Plume-Surface Studies (SCALPSS) is an imaging system used to capture 
            video during descent and landing on the lunar surface. The image data will be used to reconstruct 
            the effects of plume-surface interaction (PSI) in post-flight using a well-known technique, 
            stereo photogrammetry. The expected data from the SCALPSS 1.0 system will reconstruct the 3D 
            shape of the ground after it has been eroded by the lander plume.  This instrument covers all the 
            cameras as a unit.                                  
        </description>
